WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:01.800
True horror.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:06.380
The airplane door, belching smoke, and burning
red light.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.320
The dead talking in ancient, guttural Latin.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:16.439
A monstrous angel made of rings, wings, and
eyes whipping barbed tentacles at screaming,

00:00:16.439 --> 00:00:17.480
terrified priests.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.310
You can scarcely imagine a more hellish place.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:27.779
Bishop Franklin’s knees gave out under him
as soon as the man set foot back on solid

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:28.810
ground.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:34.730
Nearing his 70th birthday, he’d never been
a particularly tough man, but after the day

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:39.140
he’d had, he doubted he’d ever be the
same again.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:45.010
Almost being ripped into another dimension,
almost being at the center of a nuclear explosion,

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.010
seeing…

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:50.289
He threw up on the ground as the Foundation
personnel rushed over to him.

00:00:50.289 --> 00:00:53.020
Never - never - again!

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.020
*

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:58.109
Just eight hours earlier, Bishop Franklin
had been getting on with his Friday preparations.

00:00:58.109 --> 00:01:02.770
They had mass coming up this weekend, so he
was doing the rounds of the cathedral, putting

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:05.210
out new candles, and straightening pews.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:10.480
He was nearly done, ready to get on with the
rest of his morning, when he saw the two suited

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.720
figures entering the cathedral.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.280
He shuffled over to them, trying to explain
that they were closed, but quickly faltered

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.310
when he saw the grave looks on their faces.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:25.159
Just 10 minutes later, he was in the back
of their car, still holding a spare candle,

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:29.479
with agents from the SCP Foundation sitting
on either side of him.

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:34.970
They handed him file after file, each most
redacted, explaining the basis of who they

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:36.950
were and where they were headed.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.950
It was a lot for the old priest to wrap his
head around.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:45.299
He’d always believed in a higher power and
a spiritual realm, but this sounded a whole

00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:47.990
lot more serious than that.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:52.110
Monsters, aliens, other dimensions, facilities,
portals?

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.810
He questioned the agents on it.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:59.149
They just looked grimly from one to another
as the car wound its way to the private airstrip

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:01.140
in the middle of nowhere.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.140
*

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.869
Bishop Franklin had always hated flying, but
he hated it a whole lot more as he approached

00:02:05.869 --> 00:02:09.039
the airplane with no idea where he’d be
landing.

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:13.990
A small group of men was gathered on the runway
just by the foot of a Boeing passenger plane.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:17.819
It seemed like a pretty substantial plane
for such a small group of them.

00:02:17.819 --> 00:02:22.550
He was at least a little heartened to see
that none of them had brought luggage either.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:25.250
In fact, most of them were just like him.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:31.580
As Bishop Franklin approached the group, he
recognized various faces, other bishops, archbishops,

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.010
and senior priests.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.430
With him there, they totaled seven.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:38.480
The others all looked at him, not saying much.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:43.209
Bishop Franklin tried his best to start asking
questions, but two things happened in quick

00:02:43.209 --> 00:02:46.250
succession that closed his mouth very quickly.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:51.200
Firstly, the luggage hold of the plane was
opened, and two enormous shapes were loaded

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.270
into it via forklift.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:57.900
Each shape had unmistakable symbols on the
sheets covering them.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.530
Nuclear danger.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:03.310
Reeling from this revelation, Bishop Franklin
turned to the group to be face-to-face with

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:04.740
the Pope himself.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.640
He immediately shut his mouth.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.640
*

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:10.420
You may also be wondering what on earth was
going on at this airfield.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:15.431
The truth is, Bishop Franklin, along with
six other priests of Abrahamic faiths, were

00:03:15.431 --> 00:03:20.599
about to embark on the monthly flight of SCP-616.

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:25.610
Within this plane, as all of these men were
soon about to find out, exists an emergency

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:26.640
door.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.629
Covered with Satanic iconography, this door,
when opened at ground level, operates just

00:03:31.629 --> 00:03:36.349
like any emergency door, leading to the outside
of the plane.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:41.030
Although any individuals who have passed through
the door in this ‘normal’ state report

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:44.299
feeling heightened anxiety during and after.

00:03:44.299 --> 00:03:50.909
However, once a month, this door will be anything
but normal, opening a gate to… well, you’ll

00:03:50.909 --> 00:03:51.930
soon see.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:59.090
In order to mitigate the threat posed to humanity
through SCP-616-1 or The Gate, the plane must

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:04.700
be in the air at the time of its opening,
far above and away from any human settlements.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:09.030
In order to keep this event contained, the
door must be kept open for the duration of

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:13.350
the portal’s existence until it has closed
of its own accord.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.780
But holding this door open is not a simple
test of strength.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:19.519
It’s a test of belief.

00:04:19.519 --> 00:04:24.980
In order to protect all of humanity from unknown
horrors of a cataclysmic scale, seven priests

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:30.020
of Abrahamic faiths must be on board for this
monthly flight, praying for the door to remain

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.070
open.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:36.669
The ability to keep the door open, it turns
out, is unrelated to physical prowess but

00:04:36.669 --> 00:04:42.020
instead is based entirely on one’s own belief
that the door can be held open.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:47.740
As such, religious figures praying to a higher
power are incredibly well suited to the task.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:52.880
Once per year, the flight is blessed by the
Pope, and every time the plane takes off,

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.600
it must be holding two nuclear warheads in
its hull.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:01.160
Both can be remotely detonated by the ground
team ,who are to be in constant radio communication

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:02.440
with the pilot.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:08.250
Should the pilot fail to give them regular
updates on the status of SCP-616-1, the event

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:13.720
will be treated as an XK-Class End-of-the-World
scenario, and both nuclear devices will be

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:15.590
detonated without hesitation.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:16.590
*

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:20.690
But Bishop Franklin only knew about half of
this information from his redacted set of

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:25.210
documents and had forgotten half of that on
his stressful car journey.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:29.750
As he strapped himself into a window seat,
he was trembling like a leaf.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:34.550
He desperately wanted to complain about being
put into this situation, but he wasn’t entirely

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:37.120
sure who he could complain to.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:41.430
If he spoke to anyone external about what
he was about to witness, he had been told

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:46.370
by the Foundation agents that he would be
‘administered with a class-C amnestic’

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:47.460
whatever that meant.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:50.190
He didn’t really want to find out.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:55.090
Fortunately for him, the most familiar of
the faces from the group of priests sat next

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:57.210
to him in the aisle seat.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.370
Bishop…

00:05:58.370 --> 00:05:59.500
what was his name?

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:04.590
Sensing Bishop Franklin’s uncertainty, the
man reached a hand over and warmly reintroduced

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:05.590
himself.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:06.590
Bishop Pete.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:09.340
They’d met two years ago in Berlin.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:13.460
Just that small action was almost enough to
settle Bishop Franklin’s nerves as the plane

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:15.660
started to barrel down the runway.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:16.660
Almost.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.199
The plane took off, causing the old man’s
stomach to drop.

00:06:20.199 --> 00:06:23.370
Heart hammering, he looked around, spotting
the emergency door.

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.840
It was just up ahead of him, around the middle
of the fuselage.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:32.380
It would have looked like a normal emergency
exit, but for the blood-red markings scrawled

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:33.470
across it.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.699
A wave of dread washed over him.

00:06:35.699 --> 00:06:38.639
It certainly looked evil, that was for sure.

00:06:38.639 --> 00:06:42.500
Trying his best to help, Bishop Pete struck
up a conversation.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.259
He explained it wasn’t his first time doing
this.

00:06:45.259 --> 00:06:48.410
He’d been drafted in to help three months
ago.

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:52.240
It was scary, for sure, but everything was
totally fine.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.599
The Foundation had planned everything to a
T. It would have helped Bishop Franklin’s

00:06:56.599 --> 00:07:01.150
nerves, but it only made his mind jump to
the nuclear weapons he’d seen loaded into

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.930
where his suitcase would normally have gone.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:06.610
The two of them lapsed into silence for a
while.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.630
No one on the plane was really speaking.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:13.979
He supposed he should have used this opportunity
to pray, but according to his briefing, he’d

00:07:13.979 --> 00:07:16.190
be doing a lot of that very soon.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:19.690
He hadn’t entirely understood what the Foundation
had meant by that.

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:24.150
He’d been told to pray to ‘keep the door
open’.

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:25.610
What had they meant by that?

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:29.480
A bang shattered the silence as the emergency
door slammed wide open.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:34.960
In an instant, the plane went into a nosedive
as all the air rushed from inside.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:40.440
The lights went out for several seconds, then
came back on in flashing, panicked spasms.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:44.789
Bishop Franklin clung for dear life onto the
back of the chair in front of him as the roar

00:07:44.789 --> 00:07:46.509
of air rushed around him.

00:07:46.509 --> 00:07:52.629
It had gone dark outside, with shapeless clouds
swirling around him, shaking the plane.

00:07:52.629 --> 00:07:54.729
Screaming voices filled the aircraft.

00:07:54.729 --> 00:07:58.530
Not just the voices of the men on board but
women and children too.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:02.600
Crying out in agony and terror through throats
that sounded like they’d been lashed with

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:04.909
razor wire.

00:08:04.909 --> 00:08:07.639
Then he saw…

00:08:07.639 --> 00:08:08.639
it.

00:08:08.639 --> 00:08:12.030
SCP-616-1, the Gate, was wide open.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:16.789
Smoke billowed out of it, crawling along the
floors of the cabin like an octopus creeping

00:08:16.789 --> 00:08:19.270
its way along the ocean floor.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:23.120
Red light seemed to spill out of it, but when
he tried to look through the gate itself,

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:25.570
it was like his brain wasn’t working anymore.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:30.240
There were colors there, but they were ones
he didn’t recognize, maybe they weren’t

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.319
colors at all.

00:08:31.319 --> 00:08:36.219
It was like his brain fixated on trying to
sort them into something that made sense,

00:08:36.219 --> 00:08:37.399
something rational.

00:08:37.399 --> 00:08:42.930
A hand grasped his arm, and he turned to see
Bishop Pete staring at him with wild eyes.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:46.960
The plane was going down, they could both
feel it, and that emergency door was slowly

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.339
creeping shut.

00:08:48.339 --> 00:08:51.300
They had been brought onto this plane for
one job only.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.460
To pray like their lives depended on it.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:57.700
Bishop Franklin screwed his eyes shut and
clasped his hands together.

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:01.720
He hadn’t prayed like that since he was
a little kid, but he figured now was the time

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:03.650
to use all the tricks in the book.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:08.350
He begged and pleaded in a tiny voice for
God to keep that door open.

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:13.519
It felt so counterintuitive, so backwards,
to want to keep that kind of door open as

00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:19.590
the air roared and screamed around him, but
a small voice inside him told him to persevere.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:21.459
Have a little faith!

00:09:21.459 --> 00:09:26.269
But suddenly, the Bishop noticed that the
man sitting alongside him had fallen silent.

00:09:26.269 --> 00:09:30.100
Feeling like a naughty child at mass, he opened
one eye and peered sideways.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:33.240
Bishop Pete was still in his seat but he’d
slumped over.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:34.560
He wasn’t breathing.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.649
His skin was cold to the touch, deathly cold.

00:09:37.649 --> 00:09:41.640
Then all of a sudden, his head rocked backwards
and he started talking.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.970
Not talking like a normal man, but talking
like a man possessed.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:50.779
His dead eyes rolled around in his head aimlessly
as a guttural voice rasped out of his throat.

00:09:50.779 --> 00:09:53.510
None of them were words that Bishop Franklin
recognized.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:57.529
They sounded almost like Latin but far darker
and more ancient.

00:09:57.529 --> 00:10:03.610
And the more the dead man spoke, the more
the emergency door closed.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:07.720
The Bishop started praying again, much harder
this time, digging his fingernails into his

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:11.149
palms so hard he felt them drawing blood.

00:10:11.149 --> 00:10:13.440
He needed to keep this door open.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:18.649
He had to, and he could; he believed it entirely
in that moment.

00:10:18.649 --> 00:10:22.779
The door banged back open, wider than ever,
despite the chanting of the dead body in the

00:10:22.779 --> 00:10:24.310
seat next to him.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:28.399
Nightmares swelled to the forefront of his
mind as the plane hurtled to the ground.

00:10:28.399 --> 00:10:29.399
*

00:10:29.399 --> 00:10:30.899
Only, the plane wasn’t hurtling to the ground.

00:10:30.899 --> 00:10:37.800
In fact, it was flying at a perfectly steady
altitude of 10,972m with an airspeed speed

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:39.240
of about 780km/h.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:45.490
In fact, aside from the death of Bishop Pete,
everything within the plane was going perfectly

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:46.750
to plan.

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:52.420
Deaths of priests were just an occupational
hazard of keeping this SCP contained.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:56.310
The pilot at the front of the plane regarded
the whole situation playing out behind him

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:59.240
while feeding constant information back to
base.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:02.090
Everything was going perfectly according to
plan.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.560
Until the angel appeared.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:05.560
*

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.610
Bishop Franklin wasn’t the first one to
see it.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:12.430
That was the unfortunate lot of Archbishop
Michael, who was sitting closest to the emergency

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:13.430
door.

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:17.850
He first spied it while staring through into
the void, but his screams of terror, warning

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:21.780
those around him, were drowned out by all
of the other commotion.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:26.520
It was only when the angel’s wings crept
their way through the edges of the door, and

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:30.300
the creature let itself into the cabin that
the others saw it.

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:34.360
But by this point, it was too late for Archbishop
Michael.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:39.410
The angel was not like the angels we see in
pop culture, a tall blonde person with white

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:42.540
robes, fluffy wings, and a gentle face.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:48.820
It was a shifting mass of eyes and tortured
wings, partially crawling along the ground,

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:52.150
partially floating under the weight of its
massive frame.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:55.580
It had to squeeze itself through the door
to fit into the plane.

00:11:55.580 --> 00:12:02.810
But as it did, it lashed out at the Archbishop
with a sinewy tendril and got to work, violently

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:04.029
killing him.

00:12:04.029 --> 00:12:07.089
That was when Bishop Franklin saw it and began
to panic.

00:12:07.089 --> 00:12:11.470
He wanted nothing more than to stop praying,
to let the emergency door slam shut, and keep

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:16.360
this creature away from them, but that little
voice inside his head told him that wouldn’t

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.360
work.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:22.410
If that door was allowed to close before the
gate had, then it would cause the apocalypse.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:25.399
He couldn’t have that blood on his hands.

00:12:25.399 --> 00:12:29.709
So he prayed, sweat pouring down his face
as the angel forced its way through the gate

00:12:29.709 --> 00:12:31.390
and into the cabin.

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:36.230
He prayed as it slumped across the aisles,
working its way along the line of men, slaughtering

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:37.950
them one by one.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:42.600
He prayed as it saw him and rose to its full
height, unfurling great wings and readying

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:43.889
itself for the kill.

00:12:43.889 --> 00:12:48.700
And he prayed as a wind more powerful than
any on earth blew through the cabin and pulled

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:51.080
the angel back through the gate.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:56.730
The emergency door slammed shut, and in an
instant, the plane seemed to right itself.

00:12:56.730 --> 00:12:59.320
No more turbulence, no more wind.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:03.260
The lights flickered once more and then came
back on steady.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.610
The seatbelt sign pinged off.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:09.670
And the oxygen masks dropped down from the
ceiling, about 4 hours too late.

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:12.980
Bishop Franklin couldn’t believe the time
when he looked at his wristwatch.

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:17.370
He had been on this plane for weeks surely,
not just 4 hours.

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:18.649
That was absurd!

00:13:18.649 --> 00:13:23.770
It all felt like a dream as the aircraft circled
around the airstrip, preparing for landing.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:26.730
Everything in the plane seemed totally normal
to him now.

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:31.149
Except, of course, for the four dead bodies,
one of which was slumped towards him in the

00:13:31.149 --> 00:13:32.260
aisle seat.

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:36.699
The plane landed, the Bishop staggered down
the stairs and threw up on the blacktop.

00:13:36.699 --> 00:13:41.350
After a few awkward moments, the pilot sidled
over to him and muttered a quick thanks.

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:45.449
‘I was real close to calling it a failure
there and having them set off the nukes.

00:13:45.449 --> 00:13:48.380
I don’t know what you prayed for, but you
did good today.’

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:50.870
Bishop Franklin didn’t feel like he did
good.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:56.610
He felt like he’d had his whole life, his
whole worldview, turned upside down in the

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:59.490
space of an interstate flight.

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:04.040
He had been moments away from either being
vaporized by a nuclear bomb or from having

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:09.070
economy seats to the premiere of the destruction
of the world as we know it.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:15.100
But just 31 days later, Bishop Franklin was
on that same flight again, praying his hardest

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:17.790
as the aircraft dropped into freefall.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:21.839
If there was one thing that the Foundation
noticed about working with religious leaders,

00:14:21.839 --> 00:14:26.370
it was that they had a real determination
to keep coming back to help keep the world

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:27.370
safe.

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:31.920
What the Foundation didn’t have the heart
to tell them was that all of the Satanic markings

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.370
on the door were actually fake.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:40.600
They had been added by researchers in an attempt
to make SCP-616-1 carry more significance

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.400
for those in the aircraft.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:47.490
Later testing revealed that it was not exclusive
to Abrahamic faiths, or any faith groups for

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:51.200
that matter, that they could keep the gate
open.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.730
Anyone who believed they could do it was capable
of it.

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:58.750
Faith leaders, however, are still being utilized,
and the blessing is still being performed

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:01.130
by the Pope on a yearly basis.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:06.460
It has been found that these external rituals,
while not necessarily directly impactful,

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:11.750
have strengthened the belief and resolve of
those inside the plane, yielding fewer casualties

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:13.829
and shorter durations.

00:15:13.829 --> 00:15:17.850
Various experiments have been conducted to
see beyond the ‘event horizon’ of the

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:18.850
gate.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.940
To see what’s on the other side.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:25.490
Those in the plane have reported it as having
the name ‘Paradise’ despite never going

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:26.490
inside.

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:30.579
A remote-controlled rover was sent inside
the gate on one experiment, but the footage

00:15:30.579 --> 00:15:35.720
was deemed far too dangerous as all those
who witnessed it died within two months.

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:41.759
Hopefully, you didn’t peer too closely into
the gate as you watched this video…

00:15:41.759 --> 00:15:48.060
Now check out “The Plane That Never Was
SCP-787” and “SCP-2086 Man Eating Bus”

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:48.560
for more!

